## Global Flags

{% aside type="tip" title="CI & Agents" %}
Combine `--quiet --json` for machine-readable output in CI and agent pipelines.
{% /aside %}

| Flag | Description |
|---|---|
| `--quiet` | Suppress decorative output |
| `--json` | Output structured JSON |

---

## `qql-go connect`

Configure the connection to a Qdrant instance.

{% terminal title="Usage" %}
qql-go connect --url <qdrant-url> [flags]
{% /terminal %}

### Connection Flags

{% apiField name="--url" type="string" required=true /%}
{% apiField name="--secret" type="string" required=false /%}
{% apiField name="--inference-mode" type="enum: cloud, local, external" required=false /%}
{% apiField name="--embedding-endpoint" type="string" required=false /%}
{% apiField name="--embedding-key" type="string" required=false /%}
{% apiField name="--embedding-model" type="string" required=false /%}
{% apiField name="--embedding-dimension" type="integer (auto)" required=false /%}

| Flag | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `--url` | — | Qdrant gRPC URL (port 6334) |
| `--secret` | — | Qdrant API key |
| `--inference-mode` | `cloud` | `cloud`, `local`, or `external` |
| `--embedding-endpoint` | — | OpenAI-compatible `/v1/embeddings` URL |
| `--embedding-key` | — | Bearer token for embedding provider |
| `--embedding-model` | — | Model name |
| `--embedding-dimension` | auto | Vector dimension (auto-probed if reachable) |

Examples:

{% terminal title="Cloud connection" %}
qql-go connect --url https://<cluster>.qdrant.io --secret <api-key>
{% /terminal %}

{% terminal title="Local connection" %}
qql-go connect --url http://localhost:6334 --inference-mode local \
  --embedding-endpoint http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1/embeddings \
  --embedding-model text-embedding-all-minilm-l6-v2-embedding
{% /terminal %}

---

## `qql-go exec`

Execute a single QQL statement.

{% terminal title="Usage" %}
qql-go exec "<statement>"
qql-go exec --quiet --json "<statement>"
{% /terminal %}

{% terminal title="Examples" %}
qql-go exec "QUERY 'search' FROM docs LIMIT 5 USING HYBRID"
qql-go exec "CREATE COLLECTION docs HYBRID"
qql-go exec "SHOW COLLECTIONS"
qql-go exec --quiet --json "QUERY 'search' FROM docs LIMIT 5"
{% /terminal %}

---

## `qql-go explain`

Parse a QQL statement and return the execution plan without running it.

{% terminal title="Usage" %}
qql-go explain "<statement>"
qql-go explain --json "<statement>"
{% /terminal %}

{% terminal title="Examples" %}
qql-go explain "QUERY 'search' FROM docs LIMIT 5 USING HYBRID RERANK"
qql-go explain --json "QUERY 'search' FROM docs LIMIT 5"
{% /terminal %}

---

## `qql-go execute`

Execute a `.qql` script file.

{% terminal title="Usage" %}
qql-go execute <script.qql>
qql-go execute --stop-on-error <script.qql>
qql-go execute --quiet --json <script.qql>
{% /terminal %}

| Flag | Description |
|---|---|
| `--stop-on-error` | Stop on first statement failure |
| `--quiet` | Suppress decorative output |
| `--json` | Output structured JSON array |

---

## `qql-go dump`

Export a collection as a runnable `.qql` script.

{% terminal title="Usage" %}
qql-go dump <collection> <output.qql>
qql-go dump --batch-size <n> <collection> <output.qql>
qql-go dump --quiet --json <collection> <output.qql>
{% /terminal %}

| Flag | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `--batch-size` | `100` | Number of points per INSERT statement |

---

## `qql-go convert`

Translate Qdrant REST API JSON to QQL statements.

{% terminal title="Usage" %}
qql-go convert <payload.json>
cat payload.json | qql-go convert
qql-go convert --validate <payload.json>
qql-go convert --json <payload.json>
qql-go convert --quiet <payload.json>
{% /terminal %}

| Flag | Description |
|---|---|
| `--validate` | Run output through EXPLAIN to verify it parses |
| `--json` | Output structured JSON |
| `--quiet` | Output only QQL statements, no decoration |

---

## `qql-go serve`

Start the Connect RPC gateway.

{% terminal title="Usage" %}
qql-go serve [flags]
{% /terminal %}

### Core Flags

| Flag | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `--listen` | `:50051` | Address to listen on |
| `--qdrant-url` | `http://localhost:6334` | Qdrant gRPC endpoint |
| `--api-key` | — | Qdrant API key |

### Embedding Flags

| Flag | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `--inference-mode` | `local` | `cloud`, `local`, or `external` |
| `--embedding-endpoint` | — | Embedding server URL |
| `--embedding-model` | `sentence-transformers/all-minilm-l6-v2` | Model name |
| `--embedding-dimension` | `384` | Vector dimension |

### Auth Flags

| Flag | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `--jwks-url` | — | JWKS endpoint URL |
| `--jwt-issuer` | — | Expected `iss` claim |
| `--jwt-audience` | — | Expected `aud` claim |
| `--jwks-cache-ttl` | `10m` | Key cache TTL |
| `--role-claim` | `role` | JWT claim path for roles |
| `--tenant-claim` | `tenant_id` | JWT claim path for tenant |

### Policy Flags

| Flag | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `--policy-file` | — | Path to YAML policy file |
| `--policy-reload` | `false` | Hot-reload policy on file change |

### Rate Limit Flags

| Flag | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `--rate-limit` | `0` | Max requests/sec per user (0 = unlimited) |
| `--rate-limit-capacity` | `20` | Max burst size per user |

### Other Flags

| Flag | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `--templates` | — | Path to YAML query templates file |
| `--audit` | `false` | Enable structured audit logging |
| `--audit-file` | — | Audit log output file (default: stderr) |

---

## `qql-go doctor`

Report connection and configuration status.

{% terminal title="Usage" %}
qql-go doctor
qql-go doctor --quiet --json
{% /terminal %}

---

## `qql-go repl`

Start the interactive REPL.

{% terminal title="Start REPL" %}
qql-go repl
{% /terminal %}

{% aside type="tip" title="REPL Shortcuts" %}
- `\e <file>` — execute a `.qql` script file
- `\dump <collection> <file>` — dump a collection to a `.qql` file
{% /aside %}

---

## `qql-go disconnect`

Remove the stored connection config.

{% terminal title="Usage" %}
qql-go disconnect
{% /terminal %}

---

## `qql-go version`

Print the CLI version.

{% terminal title="Version" %}
qql-go version
# qql-go X.Y.Z
{% /terminal %}
